 Nutr Metab</source><year>2005</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>26</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15735365</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1159/000084174</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fazio-Tirrozzo</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Brabin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Brabin</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Agbaje</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Harper</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Broadhead</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A community based study of vitamin A and vitamin E status of adolescent girls living in the Shire Valley, Southern Malawi</article-title><source>Eur J Clin Nutr</source><year>1998</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>637</fpage><lpage>642</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9756119</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.ejcn.1600622</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>